KVM: s390: ucontrol: Fix memslot handling

jira KERNEL-1869
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-5.14.0-741.7.1.el9_9
commit-author Claudio Imbrenda <imbrenda@linux.ibm.com>
commit 9b8e8aad5896d66005d29920cb1643076a20b172
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-5.14.0-741.7.1.el9_9/9b8e8aad.failed

Fix memslots handling for UCONTROL guests. Attempts to delete user
memslots will fail, as they should, without the risk of a NULL pointer
dereference.

Fixes: 413c98f24c63 ("KVM: s390: fake memslot for ucontrol VMs")
	Reviewed-by: Steffen Eiden <seiden@linux.ibm.com>
	Signed-off-by: Claudio Imbrenda <imbrenda@linux.ibm.com>
(cherry picked from commit 9b8e8aad5896d66005d29920cb1643076a20b172)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

